        <reimplementedby refid="class_mock_self_healing_plugin_1a540170508c663ccdaad118a5cf3f7dd3">saveCheckpoint</reimplementedby>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Save current state as a checkpoint. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Capture the current &quot;known good&quot; state for potential rollback. This should save:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Configuration</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Connection parameters</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Critical internal state</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The plugin should maintain a limited number of checkpoints (e.g., 5) to avoid excessive memory usage.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Call this after successful initialization and after major configuration changes </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Must be thread-safe </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
